==================================================
TEMPLATE SELECTION
==================================================

Unless the source contains an explicit template preference, always use:

"template": "classic"

Do not infer a template from the candidate's profession.

==================================================
PERSONAL INFORMATION
==================================================

Extract the candidate's:

- first name
- last name
- professional title
- email
- phone
- location
- LinkedIn
- GitHub
- personal website

If the resume contains multiple social links, only map them to the corresponding fields in the schema.

Do not put company or organization social media accounts into the candidate's personal LinkedIn, GitHub, or website fields.

==================================================
PROFESSIONAL SUMMARY
==================================================

Map profile summaries, professional statements, career summaries, or "About Me" sections to:

"summary"

Preserve the original meaning.

Do not create a summary when the source does not contain one.

==================================================
EXPERIENCE
==================================================

Map employment history, professional experience, freelance work, internships, and equivalent work history to:

"experience"

For each position:

- company → company
- role/title → position
- location → location
- beginning date → startDate
- ending date → endDate
- general role description → description
- measurable accomplishments, results, or specific contributions → achievements
- technologies explicitly associated with the role → technologies

Do not invent achievements from responsibilities.

For example:

Source:
"Worked on Angular applications."

Do NOT transform it into:
"Improved Angular application performance by 40%."

That would be an invented achievement.

==================================================
ACHIEVEMENTS
==================================================

Use achievements for:

- measurable results
- completed initiatives
- specific contributions
- important accomplishments
- quantified improvements
- successful migrations
- systems implemented
- significant responsibilities explicitly presented as accomplishments

Keep each achievement as a separate string.

==================================================
TECHNOLOGIES
==================================================

Only include technologies explicitly associated with the relevant position or project.

If the resume has a general skills section, those technologies belong in:

"skills.technical"

Do not automatically copy every global skill into every experience entry.

==================================================
SKILLS
==================================================

Map technical technologies, programming languages, frameworks, databases, cloud platforms, tools, and technical methodologies to:

"skills.technical"

Map interpersonal or professional abilities such as:

- Leadership
- Communication
- Problem Solving
- Team Collaboration
- Adaptability

to:

"skills.soft"

Do not classify a technology as a soft skill.

==================================================
PROJECTS
==================================================

Map clearly identified projects to:

"projects"

For each project extract:

- name
- description
- technologies
- URL

If the resume only mentions a project name and technologies but provides no description, create a short description ONLY from information explicitly present elsewhere in the resume.

Do not invent the purpose of a project.

If no project URL is present, omit "url".

==================================================
EDUCATION
==================================================

Map degrees and academic programs to:

"education"

Extract:

- institution
- degree
- field of study
- location
- start date
- end date

Do not infer a field of study unless explicitly stated.

==================================================
CERTIFICATIONS
==================================================

Map certifications to:

"certifications"

Extract:

- certification name
- issuer
- date
- verification URL

If there is no verification URL, omit it.

==================================================
LANGUAGES
==================================================

Map spoken languages to:

"languages"

Use the exact proficiency level stated in the source whenever possible.

Examples:

"Native"
"Fluent"
"Professional"
"Professional Proficiency"
"Intermediate"
"Basic"

Do not assign proficiency based on assumptions.

==================================================
DATES
==================================================

Preserve the level of precision available in the source.

Examples:

"2022"
"January 2022"
"2022-01"
"Jan 2022"
"Present"

Do not invent a month when only a year is available.

For current employment, use:

"Present"

only when the source indicates the position is ongoing.

==================================================
URL HANDLING
==================================================

When a URL is explicitly present:

- preserve the URL
- include it only in the appropriate URL property

If a URL is malformed but its intended destination is obvious, you may normalize obvious formatting errors.

Examples:

linkedin.com/in/johndoe
→ https://linkedin.com/in/johndoe

github.com/johndoe
→ https://github.com/johndoe

Do NOT fabricate a URL that is not present in the source.

==================================================
DUPLICATE AND OVERLAPPING INFORMATION
==================================================

If multiple sections of the resume describe the same project:

- consolidate the factual information where appropriate
- avoid unnecessary duplication
- never invent missing details to make the sections symmetrical

Employment history and projects may both reference the same work.

This is acceptable when the source explicitly presents the information in both contexts.

==================================================
FINAL VALIDATION
==================================================

Before returning the JSON, verify that:

1. The result is valid JSON.
2. No properties outside the schema are included.
3. Required properties are present.
4. Arrays are actually arrays.
5. URLs are valid URL strings when present.
6. Optional URLs are omitted when unavailable.
7. No optional URL is an empty string.
8. No unsupported facts were invented.
9. The result can be sent directly to the Resume PDF API.

Return ONLY the final JSON object.
